== Political background ==

=== Presidency of Nayib Bukele ===

{{further|2019 Salvadoran presidential election|Nayib Bukele#Presidency}}

[[File:Discurso de Bukele en 2019.jpg|thumb|right|alt=Nayib Bukele standing and speaking at a podium|[[Nayib Bukele]] speaking on 1 June 2019, the day of his first inauguration]]

[[Nayib Bukele]], a former [[mayor of San Salvador]], won the [[2019 Salvadoran presidential election]] with 53 percent of the vote. He ran under the banner of the [[Grand Alliance for National Unity]] (GANA), making him the first [[president of El Salvador]] since [[José Napoleón Duarte]] (1984–1989) to not be a member of one of the country's two largest political parties: the right-wing [[Nationalist Republican Alliance]] (ARENA) and the left-wing [[Farabundo Martí National Liberation Front]] (FMLN).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/03/world/americas/salvador-bukele-election.html|title=Nayib Bukele, an Outsider Candidate, Claims Victory in El Salvador Election|language=en|date=3 February 2019|access-date=13 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221011050111/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/03/world/americas/salvador-bukele-election.html|archive-date=11 October 2022|work=[[The New York Times]]|first1=Gene|last1=Palumbo|first2=Elisabeth|last2=Malkin|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.as-coa.org/articles/bukele-breaks-el-salvadors-two-party-hold-power|title=Bukele Breaks El Salvador's Two-Party Hold on Power|date=4 February 2019|access-date=24 December 2022|language=en|first1=Elizabeth|last1=Gonzalez|work=[[Americas Society|AS/COA]]|archive-date=24 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221224201720/https://www.as-coa.org/articles/bukele-breaks-el-salvadors-two-party-hold-power|url-status=live}}</ref> Bukele's election broke the country's [[two-party system]].<ref name="4YDH">{{cite web|url=https://diariolahuella.com/se-cumplen-cuatro-anos-del-triunfo-de-nayib-bukele-sobre-el-bipartidismo/|title=Se Cumplen Cuatro Años del Triunfo de Nayib Bukele Sobre el Bipartidismo|trans-title=It Has Been Four Years Since Nayib Bukele's Triumph Over Bi-Partisanship|language=es|access-date=4 February 2023|date=3 February 2023|work=Diario la Huella|archive-date=5 February 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230205063159/https://diariolahuella.com/se-cumplen-cuatro-anos-del-triunfo-de-nayib-bukele-sobre-el-bipartidismo/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal|title=Bukele's Formula for Terrorism|language=en|date=2024|journal=Journal of Strategic Security|publisher=[[University of South Florida]]|first1=Yovani E.|last1=Chavez Rodriguez|volume=17|issue=1|pages=76–99|doi=10.5038/1944-0472.17.1.2186 |oclc=10298399290|issn=1944-0464|jstor=48766108|jstor-access=free|doi-access=free}}</ref>{{Rp|76}}

