== Electoral campaign ==

=== Nuevas Ideas ===

[[File:Supporters of Nayib Bukele's re-election (June 2023).jpg|thumb|alt=A crowd of people in front of the Legislative Assembly of El Salvador holding banners supporting Nayib Bukele and waving to a camera|A crowd of Bukele supporters in front of the Legislative Assembly's meeting room]]

On 25 June 2023, Bukele and Ulloa registered their pre-candidacies with {{lang|es|Nuevas Ideas|italic=no}} for President and Vice President, respectively.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/06/26/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-reelection-constitution/26abcbd2-1436-11ee-9de3-ba1fa29e9bec_story.html|title=El Salvador's President is Running for Re-Election, Though Critics Say the Constitution Prohibits Him|language=en|date=26 June 2023|access-date=26 June 2023|newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador|archive-date=26 June 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230626230718/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/06/26/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-reelection-constitution/26abcbd2-1436-11ee-9de3-ba1fa29e9bec_story.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On 9 July, {{lang|es|Nuevas Ideas|italic=no}} formalized Bukele and Ulloa's presidential and vice presidential campaigns.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Nuevas-Ideas-confirma-formula-presidencial-20230709-0036.html|title=Nuevas Ideas Confirma Fórmula Presidencial|trans-title=Nuevas Ideas Confirms Presidential Formula|language=es|date=9 July 2023|access-date=9 July 2023|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Williams|last1=Sandoval|archive-date=10 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240110151144/https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Nuevas-Ideas-confirma-formula-presidencial-20230709-0036.html|url-status=live}}</ref> They ran unopposed in the party's primary election and won 44,398 votes.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/cuantos-votos-obtuvo-la-formula-bukele-ulloa-en-las-internas-de-nuevas-ideas|title=¿Cuántos Votos Obtuvo la Fórmula Bukele-Ulloa en las Internas de Nuevas Ideas?|trans-title=How Many Votes did the Bukele-Ulloa Formula Gain in the Nuevas Ideas Primaries?|language=es|date=9 July 2023|access-date=9 July 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|archive-date=10 July 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230710043804/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/cuantos-votos-obtuvo-la-formula-bukele-ulloa-en-las-internas-de-nuevas-ideas|url-status=live}}</ref> The TSE approved Bukele and Ulloa's candidacies on 3 November.<ref name="NBMF" />

Bukele called on his supporters to win a three-fourths majority for {{lang|es|Nuevas Ideas|italic=no}} in the concurrent Legislative Assembly election in order to allow him to maintain the gang crackdown during his second term.<ref name="BDNM">{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/bukele-dice-necesitan-mayoria-en-proxima-asamblea-para-continuar-el-regimen-de-excepcion|title=Bukele Dice Necesitan Mayoría en Próxima Asamblea para Continuar el Régimen de Excepción|trans-title=Bukele Says They Need a Majority in the Next Assembly to Continue the State of Exception|language=es|date=28 October 2023|access-date=28 October 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Yolanda|last1=Magaña|archive-date=28 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231028203010/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/bukele-dice-necesitan-mayoria-en-proxima-asamblea-para-continuar-el-regimen-de-excepcion|url-status=live}}</ref> Bukele's campaign relied heavily on social media promotion.<ref name="Henriquez" />{{Rp|362}} In a video message, Bukele claimed that if {{lang|es|Nuevas Ideas|italic=no}} lost one seat, the opposition would "liberate the gang members and use them to rise to power" ("{{lang|es|liberar a los pandilleros y ocuparlos para llegar al poder}}"),<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/bukele-pide-votar-por-diputados-de-ni-para-que-no-liberen-a-pandilleros|title=Bukele Pide Votar por Diputados de NI para que no Liberen a Pandilleros|trans-title=Bukele Asks to Vote for NI Deputies so that They Don't Free the Gang Members|language=es|date=21 January 2024|access-date=22 January 2024|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|archive-date=5 February 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240205233757/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/bukele-pide-votar-por-diputados-de-ni-para-que-no-liberen-a-pandilleros|url-status=live}}</ref> although opposition politicians have denied such claims.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/no-podemos-negar-que-es-popular-pero-un-like-no-se-transforma-en-votos|title="No Podemos Negar que es Popular, pero un Like no se Transforma en Votos"|trans-title="We Cannot Deny that He is Popular, but a Like Does Not Transform into Votes"|language=es|date=23 January 2024|access-date=23 January 2024|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Jessica|last1=Guzmán|archive-date=23 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240123174355/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/no-podemos-negar-que-es-popular-pero-un-like-no-se-transforma-en-votos|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/medrano-acusa-a-bukele-de-utilizar-un-lenguaje-de-chantaje-para-que-voten-por-el/|title=Medrano Acusa a Bukele de Utilizar un "Lenguaje de Chantaje" para que Voten por Él|trans-title=Medrano Accuses Bukele of Utilizing "Blackmail Language" so that they Vote for Him|language=es|date=23 January 2024|access-date=24 January 2024|work=La Noticia SV|first1=David|last1=Morales|archive-date=24 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240124174346/https://lanoticiasv.com/medrano-acusa-a-bukele-de-utilizar-un-lenguaje-de-chantaje-para-que-voten-por-el/|url-status=live}}</ref> In a message posted on social media, Bukele claimed that people who continue to believe in and vote for the opposition "do not see, because they do not want to see; they will not change" ("{{lang|es|no ve, porque no quiere ver; no cambiará}}").<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/presidente-nayib-bukele-sobre-los-partidos-de-la-oposicion-por-sus-frutos-los-conocereis/|title=Presidente Nayib Bukele Sobre los Partidos de la Oposición: "Por sus Frutos los Conoceréis"|trans-title=President Nayib Bukele Regarding the Opposition Parties: "You Will Recognize Them by Their Fruits"|language=es|date=22 January 2024|access-date=22 January 2024|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Griselda|last1=López|archive-date=22 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240122222332/https://lanoticiasv.com/presidente-nayib-bukele-sobre-los-partidos-de-la-oposicion-por-sus-frutos-los-conocereis/|url-status=live}}</ref> Bukele stated that he was willing to work with the international community as long as they respected El Salvador as a partner rather than as subservient, adding that El Salvador could "change".<ref name="BDNM" /> Bukele promised to intensify his security policies, improve the country's infrastructure, and promote tourism.<ref name="Henriquez" />{{Rp|360–361}}

=== Nationalist Republican Alliance ===

Ahead of the ARENA's July 2023 primary elections, Carlos García Saade, the leader of ARENA, stated that the presidential pre-candidates' names would not be disclosed for their safety, claiming that they were threatened by persons in government and by governmental institutions.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/arena-no-anunciara-a-sus-precandidatos-2024-por-amenazas|title=ARENA no Anunciará a Sus Precandidatos 2024 por Amenazas|trans-title=ARENA Will Not Announce Its 2024 Pre-Candidates Due to Threats|language=es|date=16 May 2023|access-date=16 May 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Yolanda|last1=Magaña|first2=Susana|last2=Peñate|archive-date=16 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230516222954/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/arena-no-anunciara-a-sus-precandidatos-2024-por-amenazas|url-status=live}}</ref> On 16 July, ARENA elected Joel Sánchez, a businessman living in the United States, and Hilcia Bonilla, a businesswoman living in the United States, as its presidential and vice presidential candidates, respectively.<ref name="3candidates" /><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/ARENA-presento-su-formula-presidencial-para-las-elecciones-de-2024-20230709-0011.html|title=ARENA Presentó su Fórmula Presidencial para las Elecciones de 2024|trans-title=ARENA Presented its Presidential Formula for the 2024 Elections|language=es|date=9 July 2023|access-date=9 July 2023|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Williams|last1=Sandoval|archive-date=10 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240110151235/https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/ARENA-presento-su-formula-presidencial-para-las-elecciones-de-2024-20230709-0011.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Sánchez's candidacy was proposed by the Citizen Resistance civil movement the month prior.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/la-propuesta-de-ronald-umana-y-amigos-con-la-que-ellos-quisieran-ganar-las-presidenciales/|title=La Propuesta de Ronald Umaña y Amigos con la que Ellos Quisieran Ganar las Presidenciales|trans-title=The Proposal of Ronald Umaña and Friends with Whom They Want to Win the Presidential Election|language=es|date=15 June 2023|access-date=18 June 2023|work=La Noticia SV|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador|first1=Verónica|last1=Martínez|archive-date=19 June 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230619002730/https://lanoticiasv.com/la-propuesta-de-ronald-umana-y-amigos-con-la-que-ellos-quisieran-ganar-las-presidenciales/|url-status=live}}</ref> Initially, Sánchez's running mate was Hardy García, the wife of [[Salvadoran Independent Party]] (PAIS) leader Roy García,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/organizaciones-presentan-propuesta-para-candidata-a-la-vicepresidencia|title=Organizaciones Presentan Propuesta para Candidata a la Vicepresidencia|trans-title=Organizations Present Proposal for Candidate for the Vice Presidency|language=es|date=22 June 2023|access-date=22 June 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Verónica|last1=Crespín|archive-date=22 June 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230622191209/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/organizaciones-presentan-propuesta-para-candidata-a-la-vicepresidencia|url-status=live}}</ref> but she withdrew her candidacy because she had received "threats".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/hardy-garcia-renuncio-a-su-postulacion-politica-por-amenazas|title=Hardy García Renunció a su Postulación Política por Amenazas|trans-title=Hardy García Renounced Her Political Postulation due to Threats|language=es|date=9 July 2023|access-date=9 July 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Jessica|last1=Guzmán|archive-date=10 July 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230710033822/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/hardy-garcia-renuncio-a-su-postulacion-politica-por-amenazas|url-status=live}}</ref> Sánchez's candidacy was independently proposed by the Citizen Resistance civil movement prior to being selected by ARENA.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/elecciones-2024-presidenciales-presidencia-de-la-republica-/1068555/2023/|title=Movimiento Civil Resistencia Ciudadana Lanza Perfil para la Presidencia del País|trans-title=Civil Movement Citizen Resistance Proposes Profile for the Presidency of the Country|language=es|date=15 June 2023|access-date=15 June 2023|work=[[El Diario de Hoy]]|first1=Jessica|last1=García|archive-date=15 June 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230615205005/https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/elecciones-2024-presidenciales-presidencia-de-la-republica-/1068555/2023/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 25 July 2023, Sánchez stated that he would be willing to renounce his presidential candidacy if it was what "our country and our population wanted" ("{{lang|es|deseo de nuestro país y de nuestra población}}") in order for find a more "suitable" candidate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/joel-sanchez-acepta-que-arena-ya-no-es-tan-grande-como-parece-y-no-descarta-renunciar-a-su-candidatura/|title=Joel Sánchez Acepta que ARENA ya no es Tan Grande como Parece y no Descarta Renunciar a su Candidatura|trans-title=Joel Sánchez Accepts that ARENA no Longer is as Big as It Appears and does not Disregard Renouncing His Candidacy|language=es|date=25 July 2023|access-date=26 July 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Guillermo|last1=Molina|archive-date=26 July 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230726202632/https://lanoticiasv.com/joel-sanchez-acepta-que-arena-ya-no-es-tan-grande-como-parece-y-no-descarta-renunciar-a-su-candidatura/|url-status=live}}</ref> Following the publication of a [[Francisco Gavidia University]] (UFG) opinion poll in late-August 2023 which listed Sánchez as having 4.3 percent support, Julia Evelyn Martínez, a former professor at the [[Central American University, San Salvador|Central American University]], stated that Sánchez was considering withdrawing his candidacy due to his low polling figures.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diariolahuella.com/circulan-rumores-de-que-joel-sanchez-estaria-renunciando-a-su-candidatura-presidencial/|title=Circulan Rumores de que Joel Sánchez Estaría Renunciando a su Candidatura Presidencial|trans-title=Rumors Circulate that Joel Sánchez Is Renouncing His Presidential Candidacy|language=es|date=5 September 2023|access-date=9 September 2023|work=Diario la Huella|archive-date=5 September 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230905190551/https://diariolahuella.com/circulan-rumores-de-que-joel-sanchez-estaria-renunciando-a-su-candidatura-presidencial/|url-status=live}}</ref> In September 2023, García Saade stated that he believed that Sánchez would be able to win the presidency in the second round.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/arena-le-apuesta-a-una-segunda-vuelta-en-las-elecciones-presidenciales-2024/|title=ARENA le Apuesta a una Segunda Vuelta en las Elecciones Presidenciales 2024|trans-title=ARENA Bets on a Second Round in the 2024 Presidential Elections|language=es|date=30 September 2023|access-date=1 October 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Verónica|last1=Martínez|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador|archive-date=2 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231002212013/https://lanoticiasv.com/arena-le-apuesta-a-una-segunda-vuelta-en-las-elecciones-presidenciales-2024/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 9 November, the TSE approved Sánchez and Bonilla's candidacies.<ref name="4cands" />

Sánchez stated that the state of exception "has to be stopped" ("{{lang|es|tiene que ser cesado}}"),<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ultimahora.sv/joel-sanchez-el-regimen-de-excepcion-tiene-que-ser-cesado/|title=Joel Sánchez: "El Régimen de Excepción Tiene que ser Cesado"|trans-title=Joel Sánchez: "The State of Exception Has to be Stopped"|language=es|date=20 September 2023|access-date=28 September 2023|work=Última Hora|archive-date=28 September 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230928182109/https://ultimahora.sv/joel-sanchez-el-regimen-de-excepcion-tiene-que-ser-cesado/|url-status=live}}</ref> elaborating that it "opens the opportunity to carry out abuses, corruption, [and] [[influence peddling]]" ("{{lang|es|abre la oportunidad para llevar a cabo abusos, corrupción, tráfico de influencias}}"). Sánchez promised to review economic, taxation, educational, and agricultural policies to determine which ones were succeeding and which were failing. He described the [[Bitcoin in El Salvador|adoption of bitcoin as legal tender]] as "the worst decision [Bukele's] government could have made" ("{{lang|es|fue la peor decisión que este gobierno pueda haber hecho}}"), stating that it resulted in the [[International Monetary Fund]] refusing to support El Salvador and the government losing millions of dollars.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/debemos-restablecer-la-independencia-de-los-poderes|title="Debemos Restablecer la Independencia de los Poderes"|trans-title="We Should Reestablish the Independence of Powers"|language=es|date=9 October 2023|access-date=9 October 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Yolanda|last1=Magaña|archive-date=10 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010010252/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/debemos-restablecer-la-independencia-de-los-poderes|url-status=live}}</ref> Sánchez and Bonilla stated that they would promote investment by "establishing a judicial system that works" ("{{lang|es|establecer nuestro sistema jurídico que funcione}}"), and Sánchez claimed that he was already in talks with potential unspecified investors.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/arena-elecciones-presidenciales-presidencia-de-la-republica-2024-/1095398/2023/|title="Tenemos que Buscar Inversión y que Nuestro Sistema Jurídico Funcione": Candidaturas de ARENA|trans-title="We Have to Seek Investment and that Out Legal System Functions|language=es|date=9 October 2023|access-date=10 October 2023|work=[[El Diario de Hoy]]|first1=Jessica|last1=García|archive-date=10 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010202529/https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/arena-elecciones-presidenciales-presidencia-de-la-republica-2024-/1095398/2023/|url-status=live}}</ref> Sánchez supported restoring diplomatic relations with [[Taiwan]] as he believes that Taiwan was a "better ally" than [[China]], citing better exchange student programs and trade deals with the country before relations were severed in 2018. He opposed reducing the number of municipalities,{{efn|In June 2023, the Legislative Assembly of El Salvador approved a proposal by Bukele to reduce the number of [[Municipalities of El Salvador|municipalities]] from 262 to 44.<ref name="Henriquez" />{{Rp|359}}<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Reduccion-de-municipios-se-hizo-de-manera-arbitraria-y-antojadiza...-y-aleja-el-Gobierno-local-de-la-gente-senala-Cristosal-20230613-0009.html|title=Reducción de Municipios se Hizo de Manera "Arbitraria y Antojadiza... y Aleja el Gobierno Local de la Gente", Señala Cristosal|trans-title=The Reduction of Municipalities was Done in a Manner which was "Arbitrary and Whimsical... and Distances the Local Government from the People", Signals Cristosal|language=es|date=13 June 2023|access-date=13 June 2023|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Ronald|last1=Erazo|archive-date=13 June 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230613214419/https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Reduccion-de-municipios-se-hizo-de-manera-arbitraria-y-antojadiza...-y-aleja-el-Gobierno-local-de-la-gente-senala-Cristosal-20230613-0009.html|url-status=live}}</ref> The reductions would go into effect on 1 May 2024.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Quien-gobernara-donde-estos-son-los-ganadores-en-las-44-nuevas-alcaldias-de-El-Salvador-y-los-distritos-que-incluyen-20240304-0018.html|title=El Salvador se Reduce a 44 Nuevos Municipios ¿Cómo se Llama el Suyo, Qué Distritos Incluye y Quién lo Gobernará?|trans-title=El Salvador Is Reduced to 44 New Municipalities. What Is Yours Called, What Districts Are Included, and Who Will Govern Them?|language=es|date=1 May 2024|access-date=4 September 2024|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Beatriz|last1=Calderón|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240322044912/https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Quien-gobernara-donde-estos-son-los-ganadores-en-las-44-nuevas-alcaldias-de-El-Salvador-y-los-distritos-que-incluyen-20240304-0018.html|archive-date=22 March 2024|url-status=dead}}</ref>}} arguing that it would result in parts of the country being neglected by mayors.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/elecciones-presidenciales-arena-el-salvador-/1098806/2023/|title=Entrevistas a Fórmulas Presidenciales: "Como Punto Primordial es Recuperar el Orden Constitucional": Joel Sánchez|trans-title=Interviews with Presidential Formulas: "The Primary Point is to Restore Constitutional Order": Joel Sánchez|language=es|date=23 October 2023|access-date=24 October 2023|work=[[El Diario de Hoy]]|first1=Jessica|last1=García|archive-date=26 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231026171119/https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/elecciones-presidenciales-arena-el-salvador-/1098806/2023/|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Farabundo Martí National Liberation Front ===

[[File:FMLN election campaign rally (2024).png|thumb|right|alt=A photograph of an FMLN campaign rally|A January 2024 FMLN rally]]

On 29 May 2023, Flores registered as a pre-candidate for the presidency and Werner Marroquín registered as his running-mate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/exdiputado-manuel-flores-se-inscribe-como-precandidato-presidencial-por-el-fmln|title=Ex-Diputado Manuel Flores se Inscribe como Precandidato Presidencial por el FMLN|trans-title=Ex-Deputy Manuel Flores Registers Himself as a Presidential Pre-Candidate for the FMLN|language=es|date=29 May 2023|access-date=29 May 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Susana|last1=Peñate|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529035746/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/exdiputado-manuel-flores-se-inscribe-como-precandidato-presidencial-por-el-fmln|url-status=live}}</ref> Flores was the party's only presidential pre-candidate to register,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Flores-unico-precandidato-a-presidencia-por-el-FMLN-20230528-0063.html|title=Flores, Único Precandidato a Presidencia por el FMLN|trans-title=Flores, Only Pre-Candidate for the Presidency for the FMLN|language=es|date=29 May 2023|access-date=29 May 2023|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Verónica|last1=Martínez|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529160243/https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Flores-unico-precandidato-a-presidencia-por-el-FMLN-20230528-0063.html|url-status=live}}</ref> although Jaime Zavaleta expressed interest in securing the party's nomination.<ref name="Zavaleta" /> On 16 July 2023, Flores and Marroquín were elected as the FMLN's presidential and vice presidential candidates, respectively.<ref name="6primaries">{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/seis-partidos-eligieron-ayer-a-sus-candidatos-para-elecciones-2024|title=Seis Partidos Eligieron Ayer a sus Candidatos para Elecciones 2024|trans-title=Six Parties Elected Their Candidates for the 2024 Elections Yesterday|language=es|date=17 July 2023|access-date=17 July 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Verónica|last1=Crespín|first2=Leonardo|last2=Cerón|archive-date=17 July 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230717113159/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/seis-partidos-eligieron-ayer-a-sus-candidatos-para-elecciones-2024|url-status=live}}</ref> The TSE approved Flores and Marroquín's candidacies on 3 November.<ref name="MFWMreg" /> FMLN leader [[Óscar Ortiz (Salvadoran politician)|Óscar Ortiz]] assured that the party's candidates represented the "hope and future of the country" ("{{lang|es|esperanza y el futuro del país}}").<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diariolahuella.com/fmln-afirma-que-sus-candidatos-representan-el-futuro-de-el-salvador/|title=FMLN Dice que Sus Candidatos Representan "El Futuro" de El Salvador|trans-title=FMLN Says that Its Candidates Represent "The Future" of El Salvador|language=es|date=5 October 2023|access-date=7 October 2023|work=Diario la Huella|archive-date=12 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231012112424/https://diariolahuella.com/fmln-afirma-que-sus-candidatos-representan-el-futuro-de-el-salvador/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In September 2023, Flores stated that, if elected, he would maintain the state of exception if the country's population supported it.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/manuel-flores-aseguro-que-podria-mantener-el-regimen-de-excepcion-de-ganar-en-2024-que-propone-para-mejorar-la-economia-en-el-salvador/|title=Manuel Flores Aseguró que Podría Mantener el Régimen de Excepción, de Ganar en 2024, ¿Qué Propone para Mejorar la Economía en El Salvador?|trans-title=Manuel Flores Assures that He Could Maintain the State of Exception, if He Wins in 2024, What Does He Propose to Improve the Economy in El Salvador?|language=es|date=27 September 2023|access-date=28 September 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=David|last1=Morales|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador|archive-date=28 September 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230928182109/https://lanoticiasv.com/manuel-flores-aseguro-que-podria-mantener-el-regimen-de-excepcion-de-ganar-en-2024-que-propone-para-mejorar-la-economia-en-el-salvador/|url-status=live}}</ref> He also stated that all criminals would remain imprisoned and that his government would pursue others, countering claims that the party defended criminals. Regarding corruption, Flores stated that he would combat corruption and not select corrupt individuals to cabinet positions.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/fmln-dice-que-mantendra-a-criminales-en-la-prision-y-evitara-la-corrupcion|title=FMLN Dice que Mantendrá a Criminales en la Prisión y Evitará la Corrupción|language=es|date=2 October 2023|access-date=2 October 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Verónica|last1=Crespín|archive-date=2 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231002124250/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/fmln-dice-que-mantendra-a-criminales-en-la-prision-y-evitara-la-corrupcion|url-status=live}}</ref>

Flores promised to invest US$30 million in the transportation sector and reduce the price of transportation fares for students by half, which would affect around 150,000 students in the country.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/manuel-flores-lanza-su-primera-propuesta-de-campana-reducir-a-la-mitad-el-costo-de-pasajes-para-estudiantes/|title=Manuel Flores Lanza su Primera Propuesta de Campaña: Reducir a la Mitad el Costo de Pasajes para Estudiantes|trans-title=Manuel Flores Launches His First Campaign Proposal: Reduce the Cost of Fares for Students in Half|language=es|date=5 October 2023|access-date=6 October 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Verónica|last1=Martínez|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador|archive-date=8 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231008013720/https://lanoticiasv.com/manuel-flores-lanza-su-primera-propuesta-de-campana-reducir-a-la-mitad-el-costo-de-pasajes-para-estudiantes/|url-status=live}}</ref> Flores promised to launch the "Zero Hunger" ("{{lang|es|Hambre Cero}}") initiative to combat hunger by investing US$60 million into building three "zero-hunger supply centers" ("{{lang|es|centros de abastecimiento hambre cero}}") which would distribute grain.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/flores-presenta-su-propuesta-economica-hambre-cero-tres-grandes-centros-de-abastecimiento-por-una-inversion-de-60-millones/|title=Flores Presenta su Propuesta Económica "Hambre Cero": Tres Grandes Centros de Abastecimiento por una Inversión de $60 Millones|trans-title=Flores Presents His "Zero Hunger" Economic Proposal: Three Large Supply Centers by a $60 Million Investment|language=es|date=13 October 2023|access-date=15 October 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=David|last1=Morales|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador|archive-date=23 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231023205211/https://lanoticiasv.com/flores-presenta-su-propuesta-economica-hambre-cero-tres-grandes-centros-de-abastecimiento-por-una-inversion-de-60-millones/|url-status=live}}</ref> Flores also proposed raising the minimum pension from US$50 per day to US$70 per day.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Candidato-del-FMLN-propone-bono-de-la-dignidad-para-subir-a-70-la-pension-a-adultos-mayores-20231023-0044.html|title=Candidato del FMLN Propone "Bono de la Dignidad" para Subir a $70 la Pensión a Adultos Mayores|trans-title=FMLN Candidate Proposes "Dignity Bond" to Raise the Pension for Senior Adults to $70|language=es|date=23 October 2023|access-date=24 October 2023|first1=Gabriela|last1=Villarroel|archive-date=5 February 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240205234359/https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Candidato-del-FMLN-propone-bono-de-la-dignidad-para-subir-a-70-la-pension-a-adultos-mayores-20231023-0044.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He announced his "Prosperous Municipalities" ("{{lang|es|Municipios Prósperos}}") plan to develop and invest in the country's municipalities.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/municipios-prosperos-la-propuesta-del-fmln-para-devolverle-el-fodes-a-los-municipios/|title="Municipios Prósperos", la Propuesta del FMLN para Devolverle el FODES a los Municipios|trans-title="Prosperous Municipalities", the FMLN's Proposal to Devolve FODES to the Municipalities|language=es|date=6 November 2023|access-date=7 November 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Verónica|last1=Martínez|archive-date=7 November 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231107162457/https://lanoticiasv.com/municipios-prosperos-la-propuesta-del-fmln-para-devolverle-el-fodes-a-los-municipios/|url-status=live}}</ref> Flores promised to launch investigations into all of [[Cabinet of Nayib Bukele|Bukele's government officials]] if elected president.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/manuel-flores-asegura-que-de-ganar-en-2024-pedira-se-investigue-a-los-politicos-del-actual-gobierno/|title=Manuel Flores Asegura que de Ganar en 2024, Pedirá se Investigue a los Políticos del Actual Gobierno|trans-title=Manuel Flores Assures that After Winning in 2024, He Will Ask to Investigate the Politicians of the Current Government|language=es|date=5 December 2023|access-date=7 December 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=David|last1=Morales|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador|archive-date=8 December 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231208001448/https://lanoticiasv.com/manuel-flores-asegura-que-de-ganar-en-2024-pedira-se-investigue-a-los-politicos-del-actual-gobierno/|url-status=live}}</ref> In October 2023, Flores stated that he believed he would win the presidential election in the first round, making a second round irrelevant.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/fmln-juramenta-candidatos-para-2024-y-asegura-que-ganara-la-presidencia-en-la-primera-vuelta|title=FMLN Juramenta Candidatos para 2024 y Asegura que Ganará la Presidencia en la Primera Vuelta|trans-title=FMLN Swears In Candidates for 2024 and Assures that It Will Win the Presidency in the First Round|language=es|date=1 October 2023|access-date=1 October 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Verónica|last1=Crespín|archive-date=2 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231002124308/https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/fmln-juramenta-candidatos-para-2024-y-asegura-que-ganara-la-presidencia-en-la-primera-vuelta|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Nuestro Tiempo ===

On 31 May 2023, [[Luis Parada (lawyer)|Luis Parada]], a lawyer who resided in the United States,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/luis-parada-acepta-ser-parte-de-la-formula-presidencial-propuesta-por-sumar|title=Luis Parada Acepta ser Parte de la Fórmula Presidencial Propuesta por Sumar|trans-title=Luis Parada Accepts to be a Part of the Presidential Formula Proposed by Sumar|language=es|date=31 May 2023|access-date=31 May 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Yolanda|last1=Magaña}}</ref> announced that he was running for president. His candidacy was proposed by the Sumar por El Salvador political movement. {{ill|Celia Medrano|es}}, a human rights lawyer, was Parada's running mate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Abogado-Luis-Parada-anuncia-su-candidatura-presidencial-20230531-0052.html|title=Abogado Luis Parada Anuncia su Candidatura Presidencial|trans-title=Lawyer Luis Parada Announces His Presidential Candidacy|language=es|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|date=31 May 2023|access-date=31 May 2023|first1=Lissette|last1=Mondragón}}</ref> The following day, during an interview with [[Telecorporación Salvadoreña]]'s {{lang|es|Frente a Frente}}, Failer confirmed that Parada and Medrano were both running under the banner of {{lang|es|Nuestro Tiempo|italic=no}}, adding that "it's to choose between democracy and dictatorship; if we unite ourselves behind this, we will change what is happening to our country" ("{{lang|es|es para elegir entre democracia y dictadura; si nos unimos detrás de eso, vamos a cambiar lo que está pasando en nuestro país}}").<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/luis-parada-y-celia-medrano-se-afiliaron-a-nuestro-tiempo-failer|title=Luis Parada y Celia Medrano se Afiliaron a Nuestro Tiempo: Failer|trans-title=Luis Parada and Celia Medrano Affiliated with Nuestro Tiempo: Failer|language=es|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Yolanda|last1=Magaña|date=1 June 2023|access-date=1 June 2023}}</ref> Parada had previously sought ARENA's 2019 presidential nomination.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Abogado-Luis-Parada-deja-lucha-por-candidatura-presidencial-de-ARENA--20171002-0068.html|title=Abogado Luis Parada Deja Lucha por Candidatura Presidencial de ARENA|trans-title=Lawyer Luis Parada Quits Fighting for ARENA's Presidential Candidacy|language=es|date=2 October 2017|access-date=30 July 2023|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]}}</ref> On 9 November, the TSE approved Parada and Medrano's candidacies.<ref name="4cands" />

In an interview with Channel 9 in July 2023, Parada stated that, if elected, he would review the necessity and constitutionality of the state of exception.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diarioelsalvador.com/parada-duda-sobre-mantener-el-regimen-de-excepcion/388084/|title=Luis Parada, Candidato Presidencial de Nuestro Tiempo, Duda Sobre Mantener el Régimen de Excepción|trans-title=Luis Parada, Presidential Candidate of Nuestro Tiempo, Doubts Maintaining the Exception Regime|language=es|date=26 July 2023|access-date=1 August 2023|work=[[Diario El Salvador]]|first1=Amadeo|last1=Cabrera}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/luis-parada-celia-medrano-nuestro-tiempo-regimen-de-excepcion/1076791/2023/|title=Candidatos de Nuestro Tiempo Evaluarían Estado de Excepción Según lo que Dice Constitución|trans-title=Candidates of Nuestro Tiempo Will Evaluate the State of Exception According to What the Constitution Says|language=es|date=19 July 2023|access-date=28 September 2023|work=[[El Diario de Hoy]]|first1=Jessica|last1=García}}</ref> In August 2023, Parada stated that he would suspend the state of exception, describing it as "nothing more than the current government's propaganda" ("{{lang|es|nada más la propaganda del Gobierno actual}}"),<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ultimahora.sv/luis-parada-suspenderia-el-regimen-de-excepcion/|title=Luis Parada Suspendería el Régimen de Excepción|trans-title=Luis Parada Will Suspend the State of Exception|language=es|date=8 August 2023|access-date=28 September 2023|work=Última Hora}}</ref> and an "illusion".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diariolahuella.com/luis-parada-dice-que-la-seguridad-en-el-salvador-es-una-ilusion/|title=Luis Parada Dice que la Seguridad en El Salvador es Una "Ilusión"|trans-title=Luis Parada Says that the Security in El Salvador is an "Illusion"|language=es|date=7 November 2023|access-date=7 November 2023|work=Diario la Huella}}</ref> Parada promised to remove the justices on the Constitutional Court of the Supreme Court of Justice and restore the justices that the Legislative Assembly removed on 1 May 2021.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diariolahuella.com/nuestro-tiempo-de-ganar-la-presidencia-destituira-a-magistrados-de-la-sala-de-lo-constitucional/|title=Nuestro Tiempo de Ganar la Presidencia Destituirá a Magistrados de la Sala de lo Constitucional|trans-title=Nuestro Tiempo Will Remove the Magistrates of the Constitutional Court Upon Winning the Presidency|language=es|date=30 January 2024|access-date=31 January 2024|work=Diario la Huella|first1=Édgar|last1=Torres}}</ref> Nuestro Tiempo portrayed itself as an alternative to the country's traditional political parties.<ref name="Henriquez" />{{Rp|361}}

=== Salvadoran Independent Party ===

Gerardo Awad, a former presidential pre-candidate for ARENA in 2019, sought to run a presidential campaign with the Salvadoran Independent Party, but PAIS refused to allow him to run.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/PAIS-deja-sin-efecto-precandidatura-de-Gerardo-Awad-para-las-elecciones-presidenciales-de-2024-20220718-0047.html|title=PAIS Deja sin Efecto Precandidatura de Gerardo Awad para las Elecciones Presidenciales de 2024|trans-title=PAIS Voids Gerardo Awad's Pre-Candidacy for the 2024 Presidential Elections|date=18 July 2022|access-date=31 December 2022|language=es|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Gabriela|last1=Villarroel}}</ref> Awad later announced that he would no longer seek to run for president with PAIS.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/gerardo-awad-dice-ya-no-buscara-candidatura-presidencial-por-pais|title=Gerardo Awad Dice Ya No Buscará Candidatura Presidencial por PAIS|trans-title=Gerardo Awad Says He No Longer Seeks PAIS' Presidential Candidacy|language=es|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|date=10 January 2023|access-date=10 January 2023}}</ref> Awad invited [[Mario Vega (pastor)|Mario Vega]], the senior pastor of [[Misión Cristiana Elim Internacional]], to be his vice presidential candidate, but Vega declined Awad's offer and stated that he did not intend to seek any public office during the 2024 election.<ref name="Vega" /> On 4 June 2023, Awad announced his withdrawal from the 2024 election as he did not believe that conditions were favorable for his campaign, but he stated that he would prepare for a new presidential campaign in 2029.<ref name="Awad" />

On 28 August 2023, PAIS deputy secretary Carlos Molina announced that it selected José Cardoza, an agricultural engineer, as its presidential candidate and Irma Sosa as its vice presidential candidate.<ref name="PAIScands" /> Roy García, the party's leader, stated on [[Facebook]] that Molina's announcement was not legitimate and that all of the party's candidates were invalid. He added that the party should wait and reorganize for the [[2027 Salvadoran legislative election|2027 legislative election]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/PAIS-presenta-su-formula-presidencial-en-medio-de-polemica-interna-20230828-0068.html|title=PAIS Presenta su Fórmula Presidencial en Medio de Polémica Interna|trans-title=PAIS Presents Its Presidential Formula Amidst Internal Controversy|language=es|date=28 August 2023|access-date=28 August 2023|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Gabriela|last1=Villarroel}}</ref> On 4 October, the TSE passed a resolution to deregister the party and bar it from participating in the 2024 election, rejecting its candidates in the process.<ref name="PAISrej" /> Cardoza denounced the resolution stating that it was undemocratic. Meanwhile, Roy García reiterated that PAIS should wait to participate in the 2027 legislative election as he believed that the party had no chance in winning the 2024 election and was in danger of falling into irrelevance.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/roy-garcia-asegura-que-su-partido-no-debe-participar-en-las-elecciones-2024-mientras-pais-insiste-en-inscribir-candidaturas/|title=Roy García Asegura que su Partido no debe Participar en las Elecciones 2024, Mientras PAIS Insiste en Inscribir Candidaturas|trans-title=Roy García Assures that the Party Should Not Participate in the 2024 Elections, Meanwhile PAIS Insists in Registering its Candidacies|language=es|date=4 October 2023|access-date=5 October 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Verónica|last1=Martínez|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador}}</ref>

=== Other parties ===

The [[Salvadoran Patriotic Fraternity]] (FPS) selected [[Marina Murillo]], an architect, as its presidential candidate and Fausto Carranza as its vice presidential candidate.<ref name="FPScand" /> Murillo is the first woman to run for president of El Salvador since Rina Escalante ran with the Authentic Democratic Christian Movement in the [[1994 Salvadoran general election|1994 presidential election]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/presidente-presidencia-de-la-republica-elecciones-2024-participacion-politica-mujer-/1085853/2023/|title=Una Mujer Busca ser Presidenta de El Salvador, No Pasaba Desde 1994|trans-title=A Woman Seeks to be the President of El Salvador, Has Not Happened Since 1994|language=es|date=27 August 2023|access-date=28 August 2023|work=[[El Diario de Hoy]]|first1=Jessica|last1=Guzmán}}</ref> [[Solidary Force]] announced that Javier Renderos, an [[Obstetrics|obstetrician]], would be its presidential candidate and that [[Rafael Montalvo (politician)|Rafael Montalvo]], an [[agriculturist]] and former ARENA deputy of the Legislative Assembly, would be its vice presidential candidate.<ref name="FScand" /> Both parties' candidates were approved by the TSE on 9 November 2023.<ref name="4cands" />

Prior to Bukele's registration as a presidential pre-candidate with Nuevas Ideas on 26 June 2023, some [[Grand Alliance for National Unity]] (GANA) leaders believed that Bukele could seek re-election with GANA rather than Nuevas Ideas as he was initially elected in 2019 as a member of GANA.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/gana-no-descarta-una-coalicion-para-respaldar-a-bukele-en-una-posible-candidatura-presidencial|title=GANA no Descarta una Coalición para Respaldar a Bukele en una Posible Candidatura Presidencial|trans-title=GANA does not Discard a Coalition to Support Bukele in a Possible Presidential Candidacy|language=es|date=19 September 2022|access-date=26 June 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Verónica|last1=Crespín}}</ref> In July 2022, [[Guillermo Gallegos]], a deputy of GANA in the Legislative Assembly, stated that the party would endorse Bukele's re-election campaign if he ran under the banner of another party instead of GANA.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/GANA-apoyara-la-reeleccion-de-Bukele-aunque-cambie-de-partido-20220711-0043.html|title=GANA Apoyará la Reelección de Bukele Aunque Cambie de Partido|trans-title=GANA Supports the Re-Election of Bukele if He Changes Party|language=es|date=11 July 2022|first1=Denni|last1=Portillo|first2=Gabriela|last2=Villarroel|work=[[El Diario de Hoy]]|access-date=21 March 2023}}</ref> On 16 June 2023, Gallegos stated that GANA would not participate in the presidential election unless Bukele was the party's candidate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/diputado-guillermo-gallegos-al-unico-candidato-presidencial-que-podemos-llevar-es-a-nayib-bukele/|title=Diputado Guillermo Gallegos: "Al Único Candidato Presidencial que Podemos Llevar es a Nayib Bukele"|trans-title=Deputy Guillermo Gallegos: "The Only Presidential Candidate that We Can Take is Nayib Bukele"|language=es|date=16 June 2023|access-date=18 June 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Jonathan|last1=Guerrero|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador}}</ref> On 26 June, Gallegos confirmed that GANA would not run a presidential or vice presidential candidate, stating that the party supported Bukele's re-election campaign.<ref name="GANABRE" />

On 5 March 2023, {{lang|es|[[Vamos (El Salvador)|Vamos]]|italic=no}} formally announced that it would not run a presidential candidate or compete in the PARLACEN elections.<ref name="Vel">{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/vamos-convoca-a-elecciones-internas-para-escoger-candidatos-a-alcaldes-y-diputados|title=Vamos Convoca a Elecciones Internas para Escoger Candidatos a Alcaldes y Diputados|trans-title=Vamos Convokes Internal Elections to Elect Mayoral and Deputy Candidates|language=es|date=5 March 2023|access-date=5 March 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Verónica|last1=Crespín}}</ref> [[Claudia Ortiz (politician)|Claudia Ortiz]] announced her intention to be re-elected as a deputy of the Legislative Assembly and that she would not seek a presidential candidacy.<ref name="Vno">{{cite web|url=https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/claudia-ortiz-vamos-selecciones-nacionales-elecciones-legislativas-municipales-presidenciales-primarias-/1050111/2023/|title=Vamos no Presentará Candidato para la Presidencia en 2024, dice Claudia Ortiz|trans-title=Vamos Will Not Present a Candidate for the Presidency in 2024|date=28 March 2023|access-date=28 March 2023|language=es|first1=Jessica|last1=García|work=[[El Diario de Hoy]]}}</ref> She later added that winning control of the Legislative Assembly was more important that winning the presidency and that she would fight throughout the next presidential term.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/La-asamblea-debe-ser-una-prioridad-para-2024-Claudia-Ortiz-asegura-que-lucha-en-proximo-periodo-presidencial-20230531-0091.html|title="La Asamblea Debe ser una Prioridad para 2024": Claudia Ortiz Asegura que Lucha en Próximo Periodo Presidencial|trans-title="The Assembly Should be a Priority for 2023: Claudia Ortiz Assures that She Will Fight in the Next Presidential Period|language=es|date=1 June 2023|access-date=1 June 2023|first1=Gabriel|last1=Campos|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]}}</ref>

In 2023, both the [[Christian Democratic Party (El Salvador)|Christian Democratic Party's]] (PDC) and [[National Coalition Party (El Salvador)|National Coalition Party]] (PCN) announced that neither would field presidential candidates.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/pcn-no-participara-en-elecciones-presidenciales-pero-dejara-abierto-a-que-sus-miembros-apoyen-a-quien-mejor-les-parezca/|title=PCN no Participará en Elecciones Presidenciales, pero Dejará Abierto a que sus Miembros Apoyen a Quien Mejor les Parezca|trans-title=PCN Will Not Participate in the Presidential Elections, but It Will Leave It Open for its Members to Support Whoever They See Fit|language=es|date=21 August 2023|access-date=22 August 2023|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Guillermo|last1=Molina|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/pdc-no-presentara-candidatura-presidencial-en-2024|title=PDC No Presentará Candidatura Presidencial en 2024|trans-title=PDC Will Not Present a Presidential Candidacy in 2024|date=5 June 2023|access-date=5 June 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Susana|last1=Peñate}}</ref> On 16 July 2023, the PDC declared its support for Bukele's presidential campaign,<ref name="PDCBRE" /> and the PCN did the same on 30 January 2024.<ref name="PCNBE" /> [[Democratic Change (El Salvador)|Democratic Change]] did not select a presidential candidate, instead endorsing Bukele's re-election campaign.<ref name="MGTV" /> [[Salvadoran Democracy]] did not participate in the 2024 election.<ref name="total cand">{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Partidos-han-confirmado-mas-de-200-candidatos-a-alcaldes-20230721-0103.html|title=Partidos han Confirmado Más de 200 Candidatos a Alcaldes|trans-title=Parties Have Confirmed more than 200 Candidates for Mayors|language=es|date=22 July 2023|access-date=22 July 2023|first1=Gabriela|last1=Villarroel|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|archive-date=22 July 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230722090843/https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Partidos-han-confirmado-mas-de-200-candidatos-a-alcaldes-20230721-0103.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

== Opinion polls ==

{{main|Opinion polling for the 2024 Salvadoran elections}}

Various groups such as CIESCA, Fundaungo, the Francisco Gavidia University, {{lang|es|[[La Prensa Gráfica]]}}, and TResearch conducted [[opinion poll]]ing prior to the 2024 presidential election. Virtually every poll indicated significant leads for Bukele.<ref>Multiple sources:
* {{cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/world-nation/story/2023-10-27/el-salvadors-president-bukele-registers-for-2024-reelection-unconstitutionally-critics-say|title=El Salvador's President Bukele Registers for 2024 Re-Election — Which the Constitution Doesn't Allow|language=en|date=27 October 2023|access-date=27 October 2023|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|first1=Marcos|last1=Alemán|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador}}
* {{cite web|url=https://www.contrapunto.com.sv/encuesta-ufg-bukele-y-ni-dominarian-todas-las-elecciones-en-2024/|title=Encuesta UFG: Bukele y NI Dominarían Todas las Elecciones en 2024|trans-title=UFG Poll: Bukele and NI Dominate All the 2024 Elections|language=es|date=28 August 2023|access-date=28 August 2023|work=Contra Punto}}
* {{cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2023-08-23/why-i-support-president-bukele-el-salvador-the-scourge-of-gangs-and-corrupt-politicians|title=Why I Support Salvadoran President Bukele, the Scourge of Gangs and Corrupt Politicians|language=en|date=23 August 2023|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|first1=Randy|last1=Ertll|location=[[Los Angeles]], California|url-access=subscription|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230823115117/https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2023-08-23/why-i-support-president-bukele-el-salvador-the-scourge-of-gangs-and-corrupt-politicians|archive-date=23 August 2023|url-status=live}}
* {{cite web|url=https://www.elsalvador.com/opinion/editoriales/encuesta-de-poblacion-activa-/1014401/2022/|title=La Última Encuesta del CEC–UFG: Reelección, Coyuntura Política y Preferencias Electorales|trans-title=The Most Recent Poll from CEC–UFG: Re-Election, Political Situation, and Electoral Preferences|language=es|date=10 November 2022|access-date=12 November 2022|first1=Óscar|last1=Picardo Joao|work=[[El Diario de Hoy]]|archive-date=11 November 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221111005344/https://www.elsalvador.com/opinion/editoriales/encuesta-de-poblacion-activa-/1014401/2022/|url-status=live}}</ref> Additionally, opinion polling was conducted to ask whether Salvadorans supported Bukele's re-election; virtually every poll indicated that a large majority of Salvadorans would support Bukele's re-election.<ref>Multiple sources:
* {{cite web|last1=Penna|first1=Carlos|date=31 May 2023|title=Jun/23 El Salvador: 4 Años de Gobierno 92% lo Aprueba|trans-title=Jun/23 El Salvador: 4 Years of Government 92% Approve|url=https://www.tresearch.mx/post/el-salvador-reeleccion-nayib-bukele|access-date=26 November 2022|work=TResearch|language=es}}
* {{cite web|last1=Rentiera|first1=Nelson|date=14 March 2023|title=Despite Constitutional Ban, Salvadoran Leader Heavily Favored for Re-Election, Poll Shows|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/despite-constitutional-ban-salvadoran-leader-heavily-favored-reelection-poll-2023-03-14/|access-date=15 March 2023|work=[[Reuters]]|language=en|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador}}
* {{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/-El-75.6--apoya-la-reeleccion-de-Bukele-de-2024-segun-encuesta-de-la-UFG-20230606-0070.html|title=El 75.6% Apoya la Reelección de Bukele de 2024, Según Encuesta de la UFG|trans-title=75.6% Support the Re-Election of Bukele in 2024, According to Poll from UFG|language=es|date=6 June 2023|access-date=6 June 2023|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Gabriela|last1=Villarroel|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230607123408/https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/-El-75.6--apoya-la-reeleccion-de-Bukele-de-2024-segun-encuesta-de-la-UFG-20230606-0070.html|archive-date=7 June 2023|url-status=dead}}</ref> Many [[Salvadoran Americans]] also supported Bukele's re-election.<ref>Multiple sources:
* {{cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/espanol/california/articulo/2022-07-12/entre-el-populismo-y-la-constitucion-bukele-busca-la-reeleccion-apelando-al-apoyo-de-la-diaspora-salvadorena|title=Entre el Populismo y la Constitución: Bukele Busca la Reelección Apelando al Apoyo de la Diáspora Salvadoreña|trans-title=Between Populism and the Constitution: Bukele Seeks Re-Election Appealing to the Support of the Salvadoran Diaspora|language=es|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|date=12 July 2022|location=[[Los Angeles]], California|first1=Soudi|last1=Jiménez}}
* {{cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-10-21/el-salvador-president-bukele-re-election-bid-stokes-fears-in-los-angeles|title=El Salvador President Bukele's Re-Election Bid Stokes L.A. Immigrants' Fears of New Civil War|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|date=21 October 2022|access-date=24 October 2022|first1=Soudi|last1=Jiménez}}
* {{cite web|url=https://diariolahuella.com/salvadorenos-en-el-exterior-respaldan-la-reeleccion-del-presidente-nayib-bukele-segun-ciesca/|title=Salvadoreños en el Exterior Respaldan la Reelección del Presidente Nayib Bukele, Según CIESCA|trans-title=Salvadorans Abroad Support the Re-Election of President Nayib Bukele, According to CIESCA|language=es|date=11 November 2022|access-date=1 January 2023|work=Diario la Huella|first1=Édgar|last1=Torres}}</ref> Those who supported Bukele's re-election believed that his continuity in office was necessary to preserve the security policies he implemented. Conversely, opponents of re-election argued that re-election itself was a threat to democracy.<ref name="Henriquez" />{{Rp|353}}

