== Results ==

The TSE published the presidential election's final results on 9 February 2024 and formally ratified the results on 17 February; Bukele (NI) won with 84.65 percent of the vote<ref name="Final Results P">{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/en-vivo-cierre-de-escrutinio-final-de-la-eleccion-de-presidente-y-vicepresidente-2024|title=En Vivo: Cierre de Escrutinio Final de la Elección de Presidente y Vicepresidente 2024|trans-title=Live: The Final Scrutiny of the 2024 Election for President and Vice President Closes|language=es|date=9 February 2024|access-date=9 February 2024|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://diario.elmundo.sv/politica/tse-declara-en-firme-el-triunfo-de-bukele|title=TSE Declara en Firme el Triunfo de Bukele|trans-title=TSE Firmly Declares Bukele's Triumph|language=es|date=17 February 2024|access-date=17 February 2024|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Ulevi|last1=Alemán}}</ref> accounting for around 43 percent of all registered voters.<ref name="Henriquez" />{{Rp|360}} Bukele was the first presidential candidate in Salvadoran history to receive more than two million votes.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lanoticiasv.com/nayib-bukele-supera-los-dos-millones-de-votos-con-mas-del-70-en-el-escrutinio-final/|title=Nayib Bukele Supera los Dos Millones de Votos, con Más del 70% en el Escrutinio Final|trans-title=Nayib Bukele Surpasses Two Million Votes, with More than 70% of the Final Scrutiny|language=es|date=8 February 2024|access-date=8 February 2024|work=La Noticia SV|first1=Griselda|last1=López|location=[[San Salvador]], El Salvador}}</ref> Among the other candidates, Flores (FMLN) received 6.40 percent of the vote, Sánchez (ARENA) received 5.57 percent, Parada (NT) received 2.04 percent, and Renderos (FS) and Murillo (FPS) each received less than 1 percent.<ref name="Final Results P" /> Turnout was 52.60 percent.<ref name="Henriquez" />{{Rp|366}}

